{"data": {"id": "7fb2a1a82a57e7d2f1a2c344c6ac7af46f1150f5054832d9d607bc99996af60c", "lineage": "7fb2a1a82a57e7d2f1a2c344c6ac7af46f1150f5054832d9d607bc99996af60c", "origin": "sample:2", "parent": null, "source": "from collections import defaultdict\n\ndef solve(data):\n    n = data['n']\n    edges = data['edges']\n    source = data['source']\n    target = data['target']\n\n    # Build adjacency list representation of the graph\n    adj_list = defaultdict(list)\n    for u, v in edges:\n        adj_list[u].append(v)\n\n    # Perform DFS to find the shortest path from source to target\n    def dfs(node, visited):\n        if node == target:\n            return 0\n        visited.add(node)\n        min_path = float('inf')\n        for neighbor in adj_list[node]:\n            if neighbor not in visited:\n                min_path = min(min_path, dfs(neighbor, visited) + 1)\n        visited.remove(node)\n        return min_path\n\n    # If there is no path from source to target, return -1\n    if dfs(source, set()) == float('inf'):\n        return -1\n\n    return dfs(source, set())"}, "kind": "candidate", "prev": "db9593e9b352dee30ecb618004e26598b56e0d411359ff28c5f4da7274111dd6", "seq": 14}
